+# Patch 0031: in-app help, pages 10 to 12 (B7)
+
+Items: the 0031 pages from the B7 page plan. Status: `[x]` done and tested in my sandbox, `[ ]` needs you.
+
+## What you asked for
+- Continue B7 with patch 31, then circle back to B6 (training mode). Small chunks, three pages per patch, each planned in the progress doc and ticked as it is done.
+
+## Steps
+1. [x] Re-cloned the repo (latest is "Docs Part 3 & Price Adjustments Part 2", which has 0030 and 0048 to 0053) and re-read `DEV_NOTES.md` and `docs/PROGRESS.md`. The copy of those two files I fetched over the web first was an old one (it stopped at patch 0003), so everything here comes from the clone.
+2. [x] Read the code behind each page before writing it: `src/lib/bundles.ts`, `src/lib/bundleForm.ts`, `src/screens/BundleBuilder.tsx`, the bundle step of `src/lib/pricing.ts`, `src/lib/sync.ts` (shared settings), the Charge flow and the bundle check in `CartPane.tsx` and `GuidedCheckout.tsx`, `src/lib/lookup.ts`; `src/screens/Pay.tsx`, `src/lib/payUi.ts`, `src/lib/saleBuilder.ts`, `src/lib/zeller.ts`, `src/zellerBridge.tsx`, `src/lib/responseCodes.ts`, `src/lib/fees.ts`, `src/screens/Diagnostics.tsx`, `src/lib/screensaver.ts` (`paymentActive`), `src/lib/posLock.ts`, `src/lib/staffAuth.ts`, `src/lib/simpleLabels.ts`, `src/lib/uiMode.ts`, `src/lib/adjustPerms.ts` (who can open Settings), and the tests that cover them.
+3. [x] `help/sales/bundles.md`: who can build deals, the editor step by step, recommended pairs, the cart card and the check before payment, how the POS picks between deals (with worked examples), dates, sharing between registers, two flowcharts, a fault checklist.
+4. [x] `help/pay/index.md`: the Payment screen, the four ways to pay, part payments, what happens when it is paid, what Back does once money has been taken, why the cart locks, one flowchart, fault checklist. It describes cash, gift card and split briefly because their own pages come in 0032.
+5. [x] `help/pay/card.md`: taking a card payment, the waiting strip, Cancel, Not approved, Payment status unknown (and the two manual buttons), Reader not ready, fees, one flowchart, fault checklist.
+6. [x] `npm run help:build` (12 pages, no problems) and `help/help.json` rewritten. All three flowcharts also parse with the in-app drawing's own parser.
+7. [x] Tests: the help tests, including the citation check, and `tests/payui.test.ts` (49 tests) pass. No new tests: these are pages only. I did not run the whole suite this time.
+8. [x] `docs/PROGRESS.md`: patch log row, the 0031 pages ticked, a "links owed" line, N21 widened, and a new non-blocking question N29.
+9. [ ] You: N21 now also covers these three pages. N29 is a question (below).
+
+## Things I noticed while reading the code (not changed here)
+- **Shared settings are pushed once and never retried** (N29). Saving a bundle deal calls `void pushSharedSettings().catch(() => {})`. If the register is offline then, the deal stays on that register only. The same is true of staff, fees, cash rounding, the PIN requirement and the price adjustment limits. The bundles page says so.
+- **Cancelling a part-paid sale does not put money back on a gift card.** The gift card is charged the moment you choose it, and the cancel message tells staff to return cash and gift card payments by hand. The Payment page says the same.
+- **The reader messages name screens that do not exist by those names.** They say *Diagnostics ▸ Zeller ▸ Setup* (the screen message) and *More ▸ Support ▸ Zeller* (the notification). The real path is More ▸ Support & diagnostics ▸ **Setup (pair terminal)**. The card page quotes the message and gives the real path.
+- **The decline sheet always offers Try card again**, even for codes that say to contact Zeller (`retryable` is worked out in `responseCodes.ts` but nothing reads it).
+- **A cancel on the terminal itself shows no message** (the result is `CANCELLED`, so the screen just returns to the payment buttons). That seems right, and the page says it.
+- **A deal that saves $0 is skipped silently**, for example a **Set price** at or above what the items cost. The editor does not warn about it. The page lists it in the fault checklist.
